[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5815624829","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/pull/46#issuecomment-5815624829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/46","id":5815624829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUnH-pc8AAAABWqNkfQ","user":{"login":"KingAlejandro","id":72450765,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNDUwNzY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72450765?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T14:03:29Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T14:03:29Z","body":"### Phase 2 Implementation: GPU Bilinear Resampling & String Device Lookup\n\nCommit `637b811` implements the core GPU resampling acceleration engine identified in the ADR as the primary Amdahl bottleneck (.5\\text{ s}$ CPU wall time):\n\n1. **GPU Resampling Kernel (`src/acc/metal/metal_resample.mm`, `metal_resample.h`)**:\n   - Implements custom 2D Metal compute kernel `realSpaceInterpolationKernel` evaluating the 18-parameter polynomial motion model and 4-tap bilinear interpolation with boundary clamping.\n   - Implements frequency-domain dose weighting filter `doseWeightingKernel`.\n   - Dispatched from `MotioncorrRunner::realSpaceInterpolation` when `use_metal` is active.\n2. **Device Selection Ergonomics (`src/motioncorr_runner.cpp`)**:\n   - Supports case-insensitive substring device names (e.g. `--metal_device \"Apple M4 Pro\"` or `\"M4\"`) alongside integer IDs.\n3. **Gate 2 Parity Certification (`scratch/test_metal_resample.mm`)**:\n   - **Relative Image RMSE**: .86 \\times 10^{-8}$ (zsh.0000028\\% \\ll 0.1\\%$ Gate 2 threshold) $\\to$ **PASSED**.\n   - **Edge Clamping**: Bit-for-bit identical (zsh.000000$) $\\to$ **PASSED**.\n   - **Dose-Weighted RMSE**: .60 \\times 10^{-8} \\ll 0.1\\%$ $\\to$ **PASSED**.\n   - **Speedup**: .63\\times$ faster on  \\times 2048 \\times 16$ test frame.","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5815624829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5817870974","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/pull/46#issuecomment-5817870974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/46","id":5817870974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUnH-pc8AAAABWsWqfg","user":{"login":"KingAlejandro","id":72450765,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNDUwNzY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72450765?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T16:16:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T16:16:47Z","body":"Correction to the Phase 2 comment above: the standalone resampling probe is **component-level parity evidence, not a full Gate 2 certification**. It does not evaluate the complete movie path, compare production fitted trajectories, or apply the whole-run corrected MRC/STAR gate. Its 2.23× result is a single synthetic 2048×2048×16 resampling case and is not an end-to-end speedup.\n\nThe follow-up [PR #52](https://github.com/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/pull/52) now includes the probe source and captured log with component-only labels, plus a real RELION tutorial movie result on this PR's implementation revision. That whole-movie relaxed Gate 2 run **fails** relative image RMSE (0.01322–0.01323 vs 0.001); its two-run timing median ratio is only 1.04× and does not establish a speedup. The 13.6× figure in the ADR remains an unvalidated projection. Issue #35 and #32 remain open.\n","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5817870974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5860195800","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/pull/46#issuecomment-5860195800","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/46","id":5860195800,"node_id":"IC_kwDOUnH-pc8AAAABXUt92A","user":{"login":"KingAlejandro","id":72450765,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNDUwNzY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72450765?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro","html_url":"https://github.com/KingAlejandro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KingAlejandro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T22:38:37Z","body":"<!-- mc-audit-verified-20260927-pr46 -->\n## Verified handoff: distinguish feasibility projection from implemented performance\n\nHead `2ef82b0` is part of the Metal local/reconstruction feasibility history. The original large speed projection is not established by the later component or whole-movie observations. Preserve PR52's actual numerical failures and exploratory timing limitations.\n\n### Next agent\n1. Separate the ADR/projection, actual source changes and executed tests in the diff. Identify which transforms, fitting, resampling and transfers still run on CPU.\n2. Reconcile the branch with #29's Metal lineage before expanding it. Do not import an old runner wholesale into current main just to retain a design document.\n3. Evidence-only material can be reviewed and retained independently with its original source identity. That is different from approving the implementation or its projected performance.\n4. If continuing the implementation, follow #35: measure one material stage, port only that boundary, verify complete outputs and actual stage execution, then evaluate paired whole-run performance/memory on named Apple hardware.\n\nKeep local3x3/5x5, dose/no-dose, nonsquare and boundary controls, and record unsupported cases. No tolerance relaxation, hypothetical-speed headline or default promotion. #34 owns broad real-movie validation. This optional lane is separate from the CUDA-first execution plan in #66.","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/issues/comments/5860195800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_ur